  "narrative": "The new discovery results leave only one threshold-relevant candidate: H13, the feature_031 contrast within high feature_038. After direction signing, the estimate is +0.173, which exceeds the 0.15 threshold, and the 95% Welch interval [0.021, 0.325] excludes zero. However, the interval does not exclude effects well below the meaningful threshold, the subgroup analysis is part of a multiplicity-heavy family, and the overall feature_031 claim already failed independent validation. Therefore H13 is kept unresolved and active with a validation request rather than accepted. All other new valid results fail the threshold and direction standard. H14 and H15 have point estimates below threshold and intervals including zero. H20 and H21 do not support meaningful effect modification. H25 and H26 decompose the earlier feature_015-by-high-feature_036 interaction and show no meaningful simple association in either feature_036 tail; H25 even has the opposite sign to its registered positive direction. This supports rejecting and closing H17 as an inconclusive or false-positive reversed interaction. H27 and H28 indicate essentially no marker association within the corresponding high-signature contexts. H29 and H30 do not support marker-marker synergy. H18 is a small and uncertain categorical contrast. No new evidence was invalid by cell-count diagnostics. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations and not causal claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 2 appraisal: H13 is the only active candidate: feature_031=1 versus 0 within feature_038>=0.7, signed estimate +0.173, CI [0.021,0.325]. It is borderline for acceptance because uncertainty extends far below the 0.15 threshold and the overall feature_031 signal failed validation, so independent validation is requested. Validation budget becomes 2 of 10 if completed. All other new valid contrasts are rejected/closed: feature_031 in high feature_018 or feature_036, feature_031 interactions with high feature_038/feature_036, feature_015 simple contrasts in high/low feature_036, reversed feature_015 interaction, feature_007/feature_058 high-signature simple contrasts, feature_015/feature_058 marker-marker interactions, and feature_024 categorical screen. If H13 validates, characterize specificity using the newly registered low feature_038 simple contrast and interpret only as a dataset-specific subgroup association. If H13 fails validation, close the feature_031 line. Continuous signature main effects H1-H3 remain deferred because the exact-value specification failed, not because the signatures are scientifically null. Untested broad screens H22-H24 and H31-H34 remain available for future exploration.",
